    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Asking for help and following a route",
     "texto": [
      "Kan du hjelpe meg? means «Can you help me?». Meg is the object form of jeg, just as English changes «I» to «me».",
      "To give directions, you can chain imperatives: Gå rett fram. Følg veien. Vis meg kartet. In many forms, the imperative is made by removing the final -e from the infinitive: å følge → følg."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
